     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "John Rawls suggested that we sit behind a “veil of ignorance,” which would prevent us from knowing who we truly are and identifying with our personal circumstances. By being ignorant in this way, Rawls argued, we can more objectively consider how societies should operate."
    }
